ForceKill - third-party attribution
===================================

This project was designed after comparing two existing utilities. It is a new
implementation; no source file from either project is copied into this
repository. The credits below are kept because the behaviour and architecture
were inspired by them.

1. force-quit (standalone Win32 "kill the foreground window with a hotkey")
   https://github.com/marcel2215/force-quit
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Marcel Kwiatkowski

   The MIT license of that project permits reuse of its structure with
   attribution, which this NOTICE provides. The full MIT text is reproduced in
   LICENSE.

2. "Force Kill Active Window" Windhawk mod (force-kill-active-window) by
   vfxturjo, https://github.com/zunaidFarouque
   Windhawk mod page: force-kill-active-window 1.0

   The mod carried no license file at the time it was reviewed, so this project
   only re-implements the ideas it demonstrated: a configurable kill hotkey, a
   protected-apps list, and live rebinding of the hotkey without restarting.
   No mod code was copied.
